# Domain Rules — Rentals

## State authority

All rental and handover state transitions are **enforced by the backend**. The mobile app requests actions; the server validates preconditions and transitions state atomically.

## Handover rules

| Rule | Enforcement |
|------|-------------|
| Photo taker | **Owner only** takes vehicle-condition photos at pickup |
| Renter role | Views and **approves** owner's submitted photos — does not upload handover photos |
| Photo parity | Both parties see the **exact same** submitted photo set |
| Immutability | Submitted handover evidence is **append-only** after the owner submits |
| Events | Pickup handover only in MVP — no return-photo workflow |

Typical rental states: `pending → accepted → pickup_pending → pickup_approval_pending → active → completed`.

Multiple renters may have `PENDING` requests for the same vehicle. Only one rental may be `ACCEPTED` or later (committed) for that vehicle at a time. Accepting one request auto-rejects remaining pending requests for that vehicle.

Owner accept creates a standard approved agreement record and reveals participant phone numbers. Pickup handover is started later, when the parties meet. After accept, either participant may cancel the rental until it is completed.

`AGREEMENT_PENDING` remains valid only for in-flight/legacy rentals.

Reject invalid transitions with domain errors, not generic 500s.

## Location

- **No maps, no map SDK** in MVP.
- Store approximate location (e.g., geohash or rounded coordinates) for discovery distance queries.
- Never expose owner's exact private/home address in public listings or discovery responses.
- Distance-based discovery uses server-side geo queries; return only approximate area to clients.

## Ratings

- Ratings require a **completed** rental; one rating per party per rental (enforce unique constraint).
- Schema: stars (required) + optional comment — no complex dispute workflow in MVP.
- Ratings affect reputation aggregates; do not expose CNIC or private agreement data in rating responses.

## Notifications

Essential notifications only (invitation, agreement, handover approval needed, rental status changes). No chat or messaging infrastructure in MVP.

## Future payments

Do not embed payment/subscription logic into rental state machine. Use separate modules/events so billing can be integrated later.
